nodes.body:
The new try in _get_or_create_session wraps only _control.connect(), not the P2PSession construction that follows. That constructor runs attach_connection → _send_connect, which sends ConnectMsg (including get_agent_metadata()) directly via the non-swallowing path — not _do_send. If that raises:
- the exception escapes past the try, up through on_new_request into the engine — exactly the ungraceful crash the PR aims to prevent;
- the ZMQ conn was already registered in transport._connections but is never closed or tracked as a session, so a later reconnect to the same peer hits assert not existing.alive → AssertionError, leaking the DEALER + monitor sockets.

